<title>SWITZERLAND: Roche declines comment on avoparcin report.</title>
<headline>Roche declines comment on avoparcin report.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Roche Holding AG declined comment on news EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler would propose next week banning the drug avoparcin in animal feed on concern its could transfer resistance to antibiotics.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not know the argumentation of the Commission, so I cannot comment further,&quot; a company spokesman in Basle said.</p>
<p>He said the additive, produced in Britain, accounted for just over 10 million Swiss francs in annual sales.</p>
<p>An EU diplomat in Brussels said Fischler would propose the ban to the EU regulatory committee.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission has received the scientific report on the use of the drug which supports concerns that the drug can cause a transferable resistance to antibiotics,&quot; the diplomat said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
